{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib proof of the asymptotic form of the Chetwynd–Hilton 1-factorization conjecture (Perković and Reed 1997, Häggkvist): for every ε > 0 there is N such that every d-regular simple graph on 2n vertices with n ≥ N and d ≥ (1 + ε) n is 1-factorizable, i.e. its line graph is d-colourable (one_factorization); the integer form with (q + 1) n ≤ q d for q ≥ 1 is one_factorization_of_ge. The proof follows Vaughan (arXiv:1010.5192) for multiplicity 1: a balanced bipartition A, Aᶜ with |d_A(v) − d_{Aᶜ}(v)| < s for every vertex (Lemma 13, here by a counting Chernoff bound with no probability theory), equitable colourings of the two sides with matched class sizes (Vizing and McDiarmid's equalisation, from the registered Vizing entry), 5-edge alternating-path exchanges until every colour class is a perfect matching, completion of the classes of the leftover inside edges by Hall's theorem, and a decomposition of the remaining regular bipartite graph into perfect matchings (Hall). Vaughan's sizes n^{2/3} and n^{5/6} are replaced by linear sizes s = ⌊a/(200q)⌋ and t = ⌊a/6⌋ with a = ⌊n/q⌋; N is explicit, N = L (512 L³ + 4) with L = 200 q² for d ≥ (1 + 1/q) n (very large). No definitions beyond Mathlib's. Two statements.",
